# Modal, toasts and the keyboard

A settings page whose name is edited in a modal dialog. The dialog closes on
Cancel, on a click on the backdrop around it, and on Escape; a click inside it
stays inside it (`.stop`). Saving posts a toast that dismisses itself after
three seconds, or at once from its own close button.

## A Note has:
    a number, which is Int.
    a message, which is Text.

## Store Toasts

State:
    Let notes be a new Seq of Note.
    Let nextNumber be 1.

Actions:
    To post (text: Text):
        Push (a new Note with number nextNumber and message text) to notes.
        Set nextNumber to nextNumber + 1.

    To dismiss (number: Int):
        Let mutable kept be a new Seq of Note.
        Repeat for n in notes:
            If n's number is not equal to number:
                Push n to kept.
        Set notes to kept.

## Component Toast (number: Int) and (message: Text)

Use Toasts.

Actions:
    After 3 seconds:
        Call Toasts's dismiss with number.

    To close:
        Call Toasts's dismiss with number.

View:
    <p class="toast" role="status"><span class="message">{message}</span> <button id="close-{number}" on-click={close}>dismiss</button></p>

## Component Tray

Use Toasts.

View:
    <div id="tray">{for each n in Toasts's notes, keyed by n's number:}<Toast number={n's number} message={n's message}/>{end}</div>

## Page /

Use Toasts.

State:
    Let open be false.
    Let draft be "".
    Let name be "nobody".
    Let insideClicks be 0.

Actions:
    To edit:
        Set draft to name.
        Set open to true.

    To cancel:
        Set open to false.

    To stay:
        Set insideClicks to insideClicks + 1.

    To save:
        If draft is equal to "":
            Return.
        Set name to draft.
        Set open to false.
        Call Toasts's post with "Saved {draft}".

    When the user presses Escape:
        Set open to false.

View:
    <main>
      <h1>Settings</h1>
      <p id="name">Name: {name}</p>
      <button id="edit" on-click={edit}>Edit name</button>
      {if open:}
        <div id="backdrop" class="backdrop" on-click={cancel}>
          <div id="dialog" class="dialog" role="dialog" on-click.stop={stay}>
            <label>Name <input id="draft" bind={draft} on-keydown.enter={save}></label>
            <button id="save" on-click.stop={save}>Save</button>
            <button id="cancel" on-click.stop={cancel}>Cancel</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      {end}
      <Tray/>
    </main>

## Test: the dialog opens with the current name and Cancel closes it

Expect that the count of "#dialog" is equal to 0.
Click "#edit".
Expect that the count of "#dialog" is equal to 1.
Click "#cancel".
Expect that the count of "#dialog" is equal to 0.
Expect that the text of "#name" is equal to "Name: nobody".

## Test: Escape closes the dialog without saving

Click "#edit".
Type "Ada" into "#draft".
Press "Escape".
Expect that the count of "#dialog" is equal to 0.
Expect that the text of "#name" is equal to "Name: nobody".

## Test: a click on the backdrop closes the dialog, a click inside it does not

Click "#edit".
Click "#dialog".
Expect that the count of "#dialog" is equal to 1.
Click "#backdrop".
Expect that the count of "#dialog" is equal to 0.

## Test: saving records the name, closes the dialog and posts a toast that leaves on its own

Click "#edit".
Type "Ada" into "#draft".
Click "#save".
Expect that the text of "#name" is equal to "Name: Ada".
Expect that the count of "#dialog" is equal to 0.
Expect that the count of ".toast" is equal to 1.
Expect that the text of ".message" is equal to "Saved Ada".
Advance time by 3 seconds.
Expect that the count of ".toast" is equal to 0.

## Test: Enter in the field saves, and each toast keeps its own clock

Click "#edit".
Type "Ada" into "#draft".
Press "Enter" in "#draft".
Advance time by 2 seconds.
Click "#edit".
Type "Grace" into "#draft".
Press "Enter" in "#draft".
Expect that the count of ".toast" is equal to 2.
Advance time by 1 second.
Expect that the count of ".toast" is equal to 1.
Expect that the text of ".message" is equal to "Saved Grace".
Advance time by 2 seconds.
Expect that the count of ".toast" is equal to 0.

## Test: a toast can be dismissed before its time, and an empty name saves nothing

Click "#edit".
Type "Ada" into "#draft".
Click "#save".
Click "#close-1".
Expect that the count of ".toast" is equal to 0.
Click "#edit".
Type "" into "#draft".
Click "#save".
Expect that the count of "#dialog" is equal to 1.
Expect that the count of ".toast" is equal to 0.
